comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-02T15:01:30.323Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate check before create: searched 'immutable history restore version', 'compaction', 'point in time', and read pm-wlqxg3, pm-h6wmtc, pm-3z0k, pm-9yfo, pm-6l2mza, pm-hib1, pm-4a7m in full. pm-wlqxg3 is the reconstruction GATE and its AC already anticipates this class ('versions it dropped are reported as intentionally unavailable rather than silently wrong') but it is the test that would catch the defect, not the product behaviour - filed separately per the standing gate-vs-product-defect split (precedent pm-0fhw). pm-h6wmtc owns retention POLICY and lawful erasure, not identifier stability. pm-6l2mza (workspace snapshot rewind) is CLOSED and concerns deleting streams, not renumbering within one. pm-3z0k is detached attestation export. No existing item owns version-identifier stability across compaction."
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
  src/core/history/projection.ts,project,"Resolves a version number or timestamp to a recorded entry; version resolution is index-relative so it silently rebases after compaction,while timestamp resolution correctly refuses with history_target_out_of_range"
  src/sdk/history-compact.ts,project,Writes the synthetic baseline entry and prunes the stream; the baseline carries only a free-text message and no structured version offset
tests[1]{command,scope,timeout_seconds}:
  node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- history-compact,project,300
